various health complications, making its management important for maintaining overall health.", "LIPOPROTEÍNA LIPASA:Lipoproteína lipasa is an enzyme that plays a crucial role in lipid metabolism, specifically in the breakdown of triglycerides. It facilitates the hydrolysis of triglycerides in lipoproteins such as chylomicrons and very low-density lipoproteins (VLDL). This enzyme is essential for the metabolism of triglycerides and is involved in the processing of lipoproteins in the bloodstream, highlighting its importance in maintaining lipid homeostasis.", "CITOCROMO P450:Cytochrome P450 is a family of enzymes that play a crucial role in the metabolism of a wide variety of drugs, including statins, which can influence their efficacy and safety. These enzymes are primarily located in the liver, where they facilitate the metabolic processes necessary for drug processing and elimination from the body.", "MIALGIAS:Myalgias refer to muscle pain that can occur as a side effect of statin use, often without elevated creatine kinase levels.", "MIOPATÍA:MIOPATÍA refers to a condition characterized by muscle weakness and pain, which can manifest as a result of various underlying issues, including disorders related to the β-oxidation of fatty acids. Additionally, myopathy can occur as a side effect of statin medications, which are commonly used to lower cholesterol levels. This condition highlights the importance of understanding the different causes and implications of muscle-related diseases.", "APO C-II:Apolipoprotein C-II (Apo C-II) is a crucial cofactor that plays an essential role in the activation of lipoprotein lipase. This protein associates with lipoproteins and is vital for the metabolism of triglycerides, facilitating the breakdown and utilization of these fats in the body.", "HEPATOMEGALIA:Hepatomegalia is a clinical condition characterized by the enlargement of the liver. This condition can manifest as a result of various metabolic disorders, including a deficiency in lipoprotein lipase. It is commonly associated with glycogen storage diseases (GSD), particularly GSDIII, and can be observed in children suffering from these conditions. Additionally, hepatomegalia may also be a symptom of Wilson's disease, highlighting its relevance in a range of hepatic disorders. Overall, hepatomegalia serves as an important clinical indicator of underlying metabolic issues affecting liver function.", "ESPLENOMEGALIA:Esplenomegalia, también conocida como agrandamiento del bazo, es una condición que puede estar asociada con trastornos metabólicos y la acumulación de lípidos en el cuerpo. Esta afección puede desarrollarse en adultos que están recibiendo tratamiento con factores estimulantes de colonias, lo que puede afectar su salud.", "DISLIPIDEMIAS:Las dislipidemias son trastornos que afectan los niveles de lípidos en la sangre, incluyendo hipertrigliceridemia y otros desequilibrios lipídicos.", "QUILOMICRONEMIA:La quilomicronemia es una condición caracterizada por niveles elevados de quilomicrones en la sangre, a menudo debido a un déficit de lipoproteína lipasa.", "APO V:Apolipoproteína V es una proteína que se asocia con lipoproteínas y tiene un papel en la unión de VLDL y quilomicrones con lipoproteína lipasa.", "OREA SOLER I:Orea Soler I is an author of the Manual de Endocrinología y Nutrición, which discusses lipid metabolism in healthy individuals.", "ILLÁN GÓMEZ F:Illán Gómez F is a co-author of the Manual de Endocrinología y Nutrición, contributing to the chapter on lipid metabolism.", "LIPASA:LIPASA is an enzyme that plays a vital role in lipid metabolism by catalyzing the hydrolysis of fats. It is essential for breaking down fats in the digestive system, making it particularly important for individuals with conditions such as cystic fibrosis, where it is often included in pancreatic enzyme preparations to aid digestion."], "parameters": {"model": "text-embedding-3-small", "temperature": 0.0, "frequency_penalty": null, "presence